      ],
      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update gradle-9 to 9.8.0-r1 or later.",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-75140 (GHSA-65r4-943x-97jj): jsoup's XmlTreeBuilder copies the whole in-scope namespace map for every start tag, so a deeply nested XML document with many namespace declarations exhausts heap memory. jsoup before 1.23.2 is affected; 1.23.2 fixes it (https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-65r4-943x-97jj, fix https://github.com/jhy/jsoup/commit/862ba2f1d48ee95609183dbcfc848c9fd7afc76a, https://github.com/jhy/jsoup/releases/tag/jsoup-1.23.2). We read every published gradle-9 package for Alpine 3.23 in the DHI Alpine repository: 22 versions, 9.4.0-r0 to 9.9.2-r0. Each aarch64 package has the same index checksum as the x86_64 package of that version (9.6.1-r3 and 9.6.1-r4 are published for x86_64 only), so we read the x86_64 packages, each checked against its index checksum, and every jar in them, including nested jars. The jsoup version comes from the Maven pom.properties inside the jar under /usr/share/java/gradle/lib: jsoup 1.15.3 in 9.4.0-r0 to 9.6.1-r6, 1.22.2 in 9.7.0-r1 and 9.7.1-r0, and 1.23.1 in 9.7.1-r1, all affected. From 9.8.0-r1, Gradle no longer bundles jsoup: 9.8.0-r1 to 9.9.2-r0 have no jsoup jar and no jsoup, XmlTreeBuilder or W3CDom class in any jar or nested jar, under any package prefix; the same search finds the jsoup classes in every earlier build. The range ends at 9.8.0-r1, the first build without jsoup; no published build ships a fixed jsoup."
    },
